p_{\min} Minimum generation probability
\lambda(t) Coupling parameter between intrinsic and extrinsic activity
\rho_P Plasticity decay rate
\rho_Q Scaffold decay rate
\rho_\eta Consolidation rate
t_{\text{crit}} Critical period onset parameter

A.4 Conventions

Convention A.1. All integrals over \mathcal{T} are taken with respect to a fixed probability measure \mu unless otherwise stated.

Convention A.2. The cost functional \mathcal{A}_t takes values in \mathbb{R}^+ \cup \{+\infty\}. The value +\infty denotes inaccessibility within any finite budget.

Convention A.3. The notation A \approx B between two agents denotes statistical indistinguishability under the protocol of Chapter 5, i.e., failure to reject the null hypothesis d_{\mathcal{A}}(A, B) = 0 at the prescribed significance level.

Convention A.4. All norms \|\cdot\| on finite-dimensional spaces are Euclidean unless indexed otherwise.

Convention A.5. Trajectory indices are continuous; s \in [t, t+\Delta]. Where discrete implementation is required, the interval is partitioned into n steps of width \Delta t = \Delta / n.

Convention A.6. The baseline trajectory \mathcal{R}_{\text{base}} is defined by \delta P_s \equiv 0, \delta Q_s \equiv 0, \delta I_s \equiv 0 for all s.

